created_at":"2026-09-21T10:37:27Z","content":"Now let me create the thumbnail workflow as an enforced rule:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# Thumbnail Generation Workflow (ENFORCED — Non-Negotiable)\n\n**Added:** 2026-09-21\n**Applies to:** ALL channels, ALL videos, ANY time thumbnails are discussed.\n\n## Rule: Outlier-First Thumbnail Design\n\nWhenever Priyanshu asks to create, design, or generate a thumbnail for ANY video topic, this workflow is MANDATORY. Do NOT skip steps. Do NOT jump straight to generating a thumbnail.\n\n### Step 1: Find Outlier Videos (vidIQ)\n- Use vidIQ's outlier search to find all outlier videos on the SAME TOPIC (not same title — same topic).\n- Cast a wide net: include different title variations, angles, and phrasings of the topic.\n- Collect at least 5-10 outlier videos.\n\n### Step 2: Extract & Analyze Their Thumbnails (vidIQ)\n- Use vidIQ's `similar_thumbnails` or manual extraction to pull every outlier video's thumbnail.\n- For EACH thumbnail, reverse-engineer and document:\n  - **Composition:** Layout, focal point, rule of thirds, whitespace usage.\n  - **Colors:** Dominant palette, contrast strategy, background color.\n  - **Text:** What text is on the thumbnail (if any), font style, size, placement.\n  - **Faces/Emotions:** Any faces shown, what emotion, eye direction.\n  - **Objects/Props:** Key visual elements, scale, positioning.\n  - **Curiosity trigger:** What makes a viewer NEED to click? What's the visual hook?\n  - **What's deliberately hidden/cropped:** What is NOT shown that creates curiosity?\n\n### Step 3: Compile the Reverse-Engineering Data\n- Create a structured summary of ALL analyzed thumbnails.\n- Identify common patterns across the top performers.\n- Identify what's DIFFERENT about the #1 outlier vs the rest.\n- Note any anti-patterns (things all outlier thumbnails avoid).\n\n### Step 4: Generate Thumbnail Concepts\n- Use the compiled data to generate 3-5 thumbnail concepts that:\n  - Incorporate the winning patterns from outlier analysis.\n  - Fix weaknesses found in existing outlier thumbnails.\n  - Are BETTER than every thumbnail analyzed — not copies, improvements.\n- Each concept must explain WHY it would outperform the existing outliers.\n\n### Step 5: Generate the Thumbnail\n- Use image generation (Nano Banana, ChatGPT, or vidIQ's generate_thumbnail) to create the final thumbnail.\n- The generation prompt must reference specific insights from the outlier analysis.\n\n## Why This Workflow Exists\n- Priyanshu's baseline for any thumbnail is: \"At minimum, better than every outlier's thumbnail on this topic.\"\n- Skipping the research step means guessing. Guessing = average thumbnails. Average = no clicks.\n- This workflow guarantees every thumbnail is data-informed, not vibes-informed.\n\n## Quick Reference for Agents\nWhen Priyanshu says ANY of these → trigger this workflow:\n- \"make a thumbnail\"\n- \"thumbnail for [topic]\"\n- \"design a thumbnail\"\n- \"thumbnail ideas\"\n- \"generate thumbnail\"\n- \"CTR image\"\n- \"video cover\"\n- Any mention of \"thumbnail\" in a video production context\n","Description":"Enforced thumbnail workflow rule: always start by finding outlier videos via vidIQ, reverse-engineering their thumbnails, then creating something better. This is a non-negotiable production rule.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\knowledge\\thumbnail_workflow.md","toolAction":"Creating thumbnail rule","toolSummary":"Thumbnail workflow file"}}]}
