{"step_index":82,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:52:45Z","content":"Now create the risk notes file:","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# Risk Notes — Audiobook / Book Summary Channel\n# Created: Sept 2026\n\n---\n\n## YouTube Policy Risks (2025-2026)\n\n### 1. Inauthentic Content Policy (Replaced \"Repetitious Content\" — July 2025)\n- YouTube now flags content created strictly to harvest views without meaningful human creative input\n- Covers: rigid template workflows, mass-produced AI slop, no original analysis\n- Stock footage + generic voiceover = NOT transformative\n- **Your risk level:** MEDIUM — AI voice + captions on images is very simple. Must have strong script quality and human QC to pass.\n\n### 2. Mandatory AI Disclosure\n- Must check \"Altered or Synthetic Content\" box for AI voice, AI images, AI video\n- YouTube runs multimodal classifiers to detect undisclosed AI content\n- Repeated non-disclosure = strikes, algorithmic suppression, YPP removal\n- **Your risk level:** LOW — just check the box every time. Zero cost.\n\n### 3. Feb 1, 2027 — Monetization Threshold Doubles\n- Watch hours: 4,000 → 8,000 in previous 365 days\n- Shorts views: 10M → 20M in previous 90 days\n- Subscribers: stays at 1,000\n- Grandfathering: existing YPP partners before Feb 1, 2027 stay in\n- **Your risk level:** HIGH — if this channel is a secondary project, you likely won't hit threshold before deadline. Will face 8,000-hour requirement.\n\n### 4. Algorithm Satisfaction Weighting\n- YouTube now weights satisfaction signals (post-watch surveys, \"Not Interested\" rates, repeat viewership)\n- Frame-by-frame AI analysis of pacing, visual redundancy, tone\n- Generic stock loops and repetitive AI pacing get suppressed\n- **Your risk level:** MEDIUM — long-form audiobook content naturally has high watch time if content is good. But AI pacing could be detected.\n\n### 5. Market Saturation\n- AI tools lowered barrier to zero. Millions of low-quality faceless channels flooded every niche 2023-2025\n- Impression pools diluted, CPMs plummeted for generic faceless content\n- Advertisers blacklist channels showing signs of automated content\n- **Your risk level:** MEDIUM — audiobook niche is crowded. Need differentiation.\n\n---\n\n## Copyright Risks\n\n### Public Domain Books\n- **Risk:** ZERO — free to narrate, summarize, or read in full\n- Examples: Pride and Prejudice, Art of War, Meditations, 1984 (depends on country)\n\n### Copyrighted Bestsellers (Atomic Habits, Rich Dad Poor Dad, etc.)\n- **Full narration / reading aloud:** HIGH RISK — essentially pirating the audiobook\n- **Chapter-by-chapter summary:** MEDIUM RISK — gray area, some channels do it\n- **Summary with commentary/analysis:** LOWER RISK — transformative use argument\n- **Key insight:** No major book summary channels have been mass-struck yet, but individual copyright holders CAN file claims\n- **Safe boundary:** Summarize + add your own commentary/analysis. Never read the book word-for-word.\n\n---\n\n## Niches Getting Destroyed (Avoid These Patterns)\n\n| Niche | Status | Why |\n|-------|--------|-----|\n| Reddit TTS + Minecraft parkour | ☠️ Dead | Zero transformative value |\n| AI Stoic motivation quotes | ☠️ Dead | Templated, no original analysis |\n| Celebrity net worth listicles | ☠️ Dead | Reused content, copyright |\n| AI historical \"what ifs\" | ⚠️ Dying | Fabricated history, templated |\n| Trivia/quiz templates | ☠️ Dead | Mass-produced, no personality |\n| 10-hour ambient loops | ☠️ Dead | Repetitious content |\n| AI emotional melodrama | ⚠️ Dying | Manipulative, advertiser-unfriendly |\n\n---\n\n## Mitigation Strategies\n\n### Must-Do (Non-Negotiable)\n1. **Script humanization** — AI draft → YOU rewrite hook + transitions → /humanizer → /ai-writing-gaps\n2. **AI disclosure checkbox** — ALWAYS check. Every upload. Never skip.\n3. **Voice quality** — Use premium AI voice or clone YOUR voice. Never use generic robotic TTS.\n4. **Appeal dossier** — Save script drafts, project files, edit history from Day 1\n\n### Should-Do (Strongly Recommended)\n5. **Differentiation** — Add your own commentary/analysis to every summary. Don't just summarize.\n6. **Visual fingerprint** — Consistent thumbnail style, color palette, branding\n7. **Revenue diversification** — Don't depend 100% on AdSense. Add book affiliate links.\n8. **Multi-platform** — Distribute audio to Spotify, Apple Podcasts\n\n### Nice-to-Have\n9. **Playlist strategy** — Group by genre/author for session binge loops\n10. **Community building** — Discord or comment engagement for repeat viewership signals\n\n---\n\n## Source\nFull research: see `cash_cow_channels_and_mitigation.md` artifact from conversation 41ca2d2f\n","Description":"Risk analysis for the audiobook channel — YouTube policy risks, copyright risks, niches to avoid, and mitigation strategies. Separated from the implementation plan to keep it clean.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\renu5\\Downloads\\priyanshu readme\\youtube\\Audiobook Book Summary\\risk_notes.md","toolAction":"Creating risk notes","toolSummary":"Risk notes file"}}]}
